<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:50%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:180%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="S3.T5.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:180%;">The gamut of Large Language Models (LLMs) included in our study.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Model Choices:</span> To evaluate the <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">generalizability</span> and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">robustness</span> of our <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">fairness-aware speculative decoding framework</span>, we consider both <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">homogeneous</span> and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">heterogeneous</span> model pairings. <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Homogeneous pairs</span> (e.g., <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt2</span> and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt2-large</span>) share <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">architecture</span>, <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tokenization</span>, and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">inductive biases</span>, allowing a controlled assessment of <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">fairness enforcement</span> when <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">representations are closely aligned</span>. For <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">heterogeneous evaluation</span>, we adopt two explicit <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">cross-model</span> setups: <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gpt2-large</span> as the <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">draft</span> and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct</span> as the <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">verifier</span>, which introduces differences in <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">architecture</span>, <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pretraining regimes</span>, and tests the framework’s <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">robustness</span> across structurally and pretraining-diverse models. In the second set up, we use <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sarvamai/OpenHathi-7B</span>, an <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Indic-language model</span> as <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">draft</span>, paired with <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">openai/gpt-oss-20b</span>, a <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">large open-weight reasoning-focused model</span>, enabling evaluation across <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">language specialization</span>, <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.30" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">reasoning capabilities</span>, <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.31" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">scale</span>, and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.32" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">open-source pretraining paradigms</span>. Our <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.33" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">model choices</span> ensure coverage of both <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.34" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">aligned</span> and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.35" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">cross-family</span> scenarios (see Table <a href="#S3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 3.3 Experimental Setup ‣ 3 Ambedkar: Fairness Aware Speculative Decoding ‣ -A Multi-level Bias Elimination through a Decoding Approach with Knowledge Augmentation for Robust Constitutional Alignment of Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), providing <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.36" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">comprehensive insights</span> into <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.37" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">fairness enforcement</span> under varying <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.38" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">representational</span>, <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.39" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">linguistic</span>, and <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.40" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">reasoning conditions</span>.</p>
</div>
